course: dictionary
lesson: 10720
title: Unwell in context
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Unwell means ill or sick, not feeling healthy. Good readers use the words around a new word to work out its meaning, and those words are the context.
explain: Look at «A cat that stops burying may be stressed or unwell.» Stressed is listed beside unwell, and a cat that stops its usual habits may be ill, so unwell means not healthy.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «I feel unwell» fits with «I feel sick», so the words match. Check that the meaning makes sense, and if it does, you have found it.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Unwell» means ill or sick; not feeling healthy.
fact: «Unwell» is an adjective, so it describes how a person or animal feels or looks.
fact: A «sick note», officially a fit note in the UK, is a doctor's letter saying a person is too unwell to work.
fact: Useful phrases with unwell are feel unwell, look unwell and be taken unwell.
exercise: «A cat that stops burying may be stressed or unwell.» What does unwell mean here? | Hungry for a snack | Very happy and playful | *Ill or sick, not healthy | Asleep in the sun
exercise: Which word means the same as unwell? | noisy | *sick | happy | strong
exercise: Lily says, «I feel unwell, so I'll stay home.» Why does she stay home? | She has a new pair of shoes | She wants to go to a party | She is hungry for lunch | *Being ill could spread germs to other people
test: Which phrase from the lesson uses unwell? | play unwell | jump unwell | sing unwell | *feel unwell
test: «The teacher said Jamal looked unwell.» What does looked unwell mean? | Looked lost in the park | Looked hungry | *Looked ill or not healthy | Looked very cheerful
exam: «A sick note is a doctor's letter saying a person is too unwell to work.» What does a sick note show? | *A person is too ill to go to work | A person is a famous doctor | A person wants a holiday | A person has won a prize
